       COHEN LENSTRA PARTITIONS AND MUTUALLY
      ANNIHILATING MATRICES OVER A FINITE FIELD

                   JASON FULMAN AND ROBERT GURALNICK


        Abstract. Motivated by questions in algebraic geometry, Yifeng Huang
        recently derived generating functions for counting mutually annihilating
        matrices and mutually annihilating nilpotent matrices over a finite field.
        We give a different derivation of his results using statistical properties
        of random partitions chosen from the Cohen-Lenstra measure.




                                 1. Introduction
  Motivated by questions in algebraic geometry, Yifeng Huang [8] derived
the following two generating functions.

(1)
   X |{A, B ∈ M atn (Fq ) : AB = BA = 0}|                   1 X      ua
